# Apovix website — configuration reference
#
# Copy to .env and fill in real values:  cp .env.example .env
# .env is gitignored; this example file is committed.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# READ THIS FIRST
#
# The site as it stands is static HTML with no build step, so nothing here is
# read at runtime. A browser cannot open a .env file, and there is no bundler
# to substitute these values into the JavaScript. This file exists so the
# values live in one known place, and so the pattern is already correct if a
# build step is added later.
#
# To actually use these values you would need either:
#   a) a bundler (Vite, esbuild) that inlines them at build time, or
#   b) to paste the config straight into a <script> tag — which is fine, see
#      the note on secrecy below.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- Firebase web app config -----------------------------------------------
# NOT SECRET. Every one of these values is shipped to the browser in plain
# text by any Firebase web app, and is visible in devtools. The apiKey is a
# project identifier, not a credential — it does not grant access on its own.
# Access is controlled by Firebase Security Rules and by the authorised
# domains list in the Firebase console. Do not spend effort hiding these.
FIREBASE_API_KEY=AIzaSyBhAN3PcT-h2F_mNuwPC7wQhKmj9Bo0dGU
FIREBASE_AUTH_DOMAIN=apovix-website.firebaseapp.com
FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID=apovix-website
FIREBASE_STORAGE_BUCKET=apovix-website.firebasestorage.app
FIREBASE_MESSAGING_SENDER_ID=847136258714
FIREBASE_APP_ID=1:847136258714:web:e32665bd9525f1c9ddbd23

# Google Analytics measurement ID. Unused — the site deliberately ships no
# analytics, and the Privacy Policy says so in section 5. If this is ever
# switched on, that section must be rewritten first.
FIREBASE_MEASUREMENT_ID=G-NTG5785581

# --- Things that ARE secret, and must never be written here ----------------
# The Firebase service account JSON used by GitHub Actions to deploy. It
# lives only in the repository's Actions secrets, as:
#     FIREBASE_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_APOVIX_WEBSITE
# Set it at:
#     github.com/miraijaz742-m/APOVIX-WEBSITE/settings/secrets/actions
# If a contact form backend, mail API key or database URL is added later,
# those are real secrets too — they belong on the server or in Actions
# secrets, never in a file the browser can reach.
